<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bazilio Olara-Okello</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1929">1929</a>–<a href="/years/1990">1990</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bazilio Olara-Okello was a Ugandan army officer who led the coup of July 1985 that overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a>'s second government. He briefly headed the new military council before handing over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tito-okello">Tito Okello</a>, and as army commander took part in the government's peace talks with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-resistance-army">National Resistance Army</a> in Nairobi. When the NRA took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampala">Kampala</a> in January 1986 he fled into exile, where he died in 1990.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Obote was overthrown a second time in July 1985 by his own commanders, <b>Bazilio Olara-Okello</b> and Tito Okello, whose military government signed a peace agreement in Nairobi in December 1985 but was driven from Kampala by the NRA in January 1986.</blockquote><a href="/empire/uganda">Uganda · Into the Present</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Uganda. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/sudan">Sudan</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=15.6,32.53&amp;year=1968" aria-label="Khartoum on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5438 1583 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Bazilio Olara-Okello"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5888 1853h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5888 1853h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=15.6,32.53&amp;year=1968">What was here in 1968? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
